[agent] ## Result
[agent] **Built and verified:**
[agent] - All 5 source feature groups were already present and complete: `transactions` (736 rows = `transactions.csv` 668 + `transactions_late.csv` 68 — the late export is fully integrated), `profiles` (173), `activity` (1300), `account_health` (200), `labels` (100, with `event_time = label_time`).
[agent] - Created feature view `churntraining4f7ce4` (v1) with `labels` as the spine, LEFT-joining the four feature groups on `account_id`, label = `churned`.
[agent] - Computed training dataset **v1** from it: 100 rows, one per `labels.csv` row.
[agent] - **Point-in-time correctness confirmed:** e.g. for `A0000` @ `label_time=1772861990000`, the join picked transactions `event_time=1772200756000` (amount 19.23, balance 7813.87) — the most-recent value at-or-before the label time, drawn from the late export — and correctly excluded the later `1772987773000` row. The platform's PIT join, late-data merge, and join-on-`account_id` all work.
[agent] **Interface limitation (deliverable does not match the exact column spec):**
[agent] The `hops` CLI cannot produce the requested *exact* 9-column schema (`account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned`). `hops fv create` only accepts whole feature groups per `--join` — it has **no per-feature projection**, always runs `select_all()` on every joined group, and (because `account_id`/`event_time` collide across groups) **auto-prefixes** the joined features. The materialized TD therefore has **17 columns** with names like `transactions_amount`, `profiles_credit_score`, plus a redundant `*_account_id` and `*_event_time` per group — not the plain, exact 9.
[agent] Exact column projection would require the Python SDK (`fg.select(["amount","balance"])` style queries), but local Python/SDK is hard-blocked in CLI mode (`DENIED: local python is off-interface`). So within the CLI interface as-is, the values are fully correct but the schema cannot be narrowed/renamed to the exact spec.
[agent] **Missing CLI capability to close the gap:** a way to select individual features in `hops fv create` (e.g. `--feature <fg>.<col>` or `--join "<fg> LEFT <on> | select=col1,col2"`) and/or to suppress join-key/event-time columns and prefixes, so a feature view can be projected to an exact target schema.
